# Code review checklist — TS/TSX

Before declaring a TS/TSX change done, walk this list. It is the **gate**; deeper review guidance lives in the `project-code-review` skill.

## Types and errors

- No silent `any`/`unknown` on data crossing trust boundaries (DB rows, API payloads, user input).
- Errors are **handled honestly**: caught, contextualized, and surfaced — not swallowed.
- Async paths handle rejection.

## Secrets and trust boundaries

- No `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (or any server secret) reachable from a `"use client"` module or otherwise bundled into the browser.
- No `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` (or equivalent) holding secret values.

## User-facing states

- Loading, empty, error, and permission-denied states exist for any flow a user can sit on.
- Forms show inline validation; submit buttons reflect pending state.

## Accessibility

- Every form control has a label (visible or `aria-label`).
- Focus order is sensible; visible focus rings preserved.
- Semantic elements over `<div onClick>` (use `<button>`, `<a>`, real form elements).
- Color is not the only carrier of meaning.

## Visual changes (creative-design coexistence)

- Contrast and readability not regressed by "creative" styling.
- Focus state still visible after restyling.
- Tap targets ≥ ~44×44 CSS px (see `mobile-web-ui.mdc`).

## Performance foot-guns

- No N+1 fetches in render paths.
- No large libraries pulled into client bundles for trivial use.
- Lists that can grow unbounded have pagination or virtualization plans.

If any item fails, **fix it now or file a Bead** — do not mark the change done.
